## Proof-Order Takeaway
1. Moser-de Bruijn is an exact automatic subset of fibbinary, but its natural
   base-4 gap coordinate is stable under n->4n, not n->2n.  LRC14 must retain
   the even/odd 2-adic phase if this carrier is used.
2. Fibbinary is the safer 2-adic normal-form language: n->2n preserves it,
   while +1 exposes the carry boundary.  That matches the Zeckendorf/path
   normal-form lane from HYP-3000/HYP-3003.
3. Raw automatic value sets fail the finite SML-period stress here.  If a
   Fermat-Catalan or linear-recurrence zero-set argument is imported, its
   ultimately-periodic index coordinate must be explicit rather than inferred
   from Moser/fibbinary membership.
4. The ACM stick/potato paper is useful only as a largest-safe-component
   geometry analogy; it does not supply arithmetic or automaton closure.
